  "result": "Perfect! All 152 tests pass. I've successfully added credit notes functionality:\n\n**New `src/credits.js` with two functions:**\n\n1. **`nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, date)`** \u2014 Generates the next credit note number:\n   - Format: `CN-<year>-<counter>` (e.g., CN-2026-0001)\n   - Separate counter from invoices (invoice counter = INV, credit note counter = CN)\n   - Restarts counter each year\n   - Handles mixed existingNumbers (both INV and CN)\n\n2. **`createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)`** \u2014 Issues a credit note:\n   - Works on 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' invoices (NOT_ISSUED error for draft)\n   - Validates amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n   - Validates amount \u2264 invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error)\n   - Returns `ok(creditNote)` with: `{ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }`\n\n**Error codes added:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Invoice must be issued, partially_paid, or paid\n- `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` \u2014 Credit amount cannot exceed invoice total\n\n**Tests added (10 new):**\n- Creating credit notes on issued, partially_paid, and paid invoices\n- Rejecting draft invoices\n- Validating amounts (zero, negative, decimal rejection)\n- Rejecting excessive amounts\n- Credit note numbering generation\n- Separate numbering from invoices\n- Year-based counter restart\n- Amount equal to invoice total\n\nCredit notes provide a complete refund system integrated with the invoice lifecycle, with independent numbering to maintain clear audit trails.",
